# `SEQUENCE-GENRE-VOCABULARY`: the allowlist row `sequence` did not have at
# 0.4, checked in BOTH directions in one file — which is the only way a
# per-genre vocabulary claim is actually pinned. Section 1 writes this genre's
# own subject words under `block`; section 2 writes another genre's under
# `sequence`. `lifeline` and `message` do NOT appear here: they are this
# genre's NODE and CONNECTOR spellings, so under `block` they get the WRONG
# WORD diagnostic instead, which fixture 284 pins.
figdown 0.1 block
node a "A"
fragment f "F" type=alt
operand o "O" in=f

# The other direction. `bitfield` is a REGION OPENER and `GENRE-COMPOSITION` composition makes
# it legal at the top level of every scene genre — but `sequence` has no scene
# to compose it into, so it is absent from this genre's row and is a line
# error here. `bundle`, `threshold` and `external` are the same shape: never
# declared by this genre, so never withdrawn from it either.
figdown 0.4 sequence
lifeline c "C"
bitfield b "Header"
bundle t "T"
threshold "80%" in=c offset=80
external x "outside"
